# ============================================================
# Environment Variables — Rural Hospitality Outreach Pipeline
# Center for Rural AI
# ============================================================
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values.
# NEVER commit .env.local or any file with real secrets.
#
# The pipeline runs as Claude Desktop skills that read/write Airtable via the
# Airtable connector. Service API keys (Serper, Hunter) are supplied to the
# skills at run time (pasted in chat or stored in the Airtable Config table per
# docs/key-handling-standard.md) — they are NOT needed here.
#
# The ONLY use for a .env.local is the optional local provisioning script,
# `npm run setup:airtable`, which builds the base schema over the Airtable API.
# If you provision the base through the client-onboarding skill instead, you do
# not need this file at all.
# ============================================================

# ------------------------------
# Airtable (only for `npm run setup:airtable`)
# Personal access token: https://airtable.com/create/tokens
#   (needs schema.bases:write + data scopes on the target base)
# Base ID is in the URL when you open your base: airtable.com/[BASE_ID]/...
# ------------------------------
AIRTABLE_API_KEY=
AIRTABLE_BASE_ID=
